# MCP Endpoint of the Local CLI Server

> For workspace problems, load `beam-diagnose-project`. For Unity setup, load `beam-unity-examples`.

## High-Level Architecture

```
Unity editor ──spawns──▶ beam server serve --enable-mcp   (one per project, dies with the editor)
                           │ 127.0.0.1:<preferred port>
                           ├─ /execute                       Unity's own SSE protocol
                           ├─ /info                          discovery: owner, version, pid, features
                           ├─ /mcp                           MCP Streamable HTTP  (Bearer token)
                           ├─ /mcp/server-card               MCP Server Card      (public)
                           └─ /.well-known/ai-catalog.json   AI Catalog → card    (public)
                           │
                           └─ writes .beamable/temp/servers/<pid>.json  {port, token, mcpUrl, ...}  (0600)

agent ──reads .mcp.json──▶ url + headersHelper "dotnet beam mcp token" ──▶ /mcp
```

## Code Mapping

| Part | File |
|---|---|
| Listener, routing, request guard | `cli/cli/Services/HttpServer/ServerService.cs` |
| Host / token checks | `cli/cli/Services/HttpServer/LocalServerGuard.cs` |
| MCP endpoint (SDK handler) | `cli/cli/Services/HttpServer/McpHttpEndpoint.cs` |
| HttpListener → ASP.NET bridge | `cli/cli/Services/HttpServer/HttpListenerBridgeServer.cs` |
| Server Card, AI Catalog | `cli/cli/Services/HttpServer/ServerCardEndpoint.cs` |
| Locator files | `cli/cli/Services/HttpServer/ServerLocatorFile.cs` |
| Preferred port | `cli/beamable.common/Runtime/BeamCli/CliServerPorts.cs` |
| Shared command runner | `cli/cli/Services/CliInvocation/CliInvocationCore.cs` |
| Tools (`beam_exec`, ...) | `cli/cli/Commands/Mcp/McpServerBuilder.cs`, `cli/cli/Commands/Mcp/McpToolExecutor.cs` |
| `mcp status` / `mcp token` / `mcp setup` | `cli/cli/Commands/Mcp/McpStatusCommand.cs`, `cli/cli/Commands/Mcp/McpTokenCommand.cs`, `cli/cli/Commands/Mcp/McpSetupCommand.cs` |
| Unity toggle | `client/Packages/com.beamable/Editor/UI/McpMenuItems.cs` |

## Business Goals Constraints

- Agents and the Unity editor share one CLI process per project, so they see the same workspace and realm.
- The endpoint runs commands with the workspace's credentials. It only listens on 127.0.0.1, accepts no browser `Origin`, and requires the per-run session token.
- The endpoint is off unless it is enabled: Unity menu **Window → Beamable → Utilities → Enable MCP for AI Agents**, or `--enable-mcp`.

## Performance Constraints

- A tool call waits for its command to finish. Commands that never finish are refused: `server serve`, `mcp serve`, `project logs`, and any `--watch`.
- Tool text output is capped at 32,768 characters (first 4,096 + last 24,576 kept). `structuredContent.events` keeps every event.
- Only `Warning`/`Error`/`Critical` log lines are returned. Progress channels become `notifications/progress` when the call has a progress token.
- Sessions of initialize-handshake clients expire after 30 minutes idle.
- The Server Card and AI Catalog are cacheable for 3600 s and revalidate with `ETag`.

## Usage Guide

### Is the endpoint up?

```
beam_exec("mcp status -q")
```

| Outcome | Exit code | Payload |
|---|---|---|
| Available | 0 | `{available: true, url, version, pid, protocolVersions[]}` |
| Not running / port taken by another process | 3 | error message saying how to start it |

When unavailable, ask the user to open the project in Unity with **Enable MCP for AI Agents** on, or to run `beam server serve --enable-mcp` in a terminal. Do not start it with `beam_exec`; it is refused.

