### Configure a client

`beam mcp setup --transport http` writes this into `.mcp.json` (other servers are kept):

```json
{ "mcpServers": { "beamable": {
  "type": "http",
  "url": "http://127.0.0.1:<port>/mcp",
  "headersHelper": "dotnet beam mcp token"
} } }
```

- `beam mcp token` prints `{"Authorization":"Bearer <token>"}` for the server at `$CLAUDE_CODE_MCP_SERVER_URL` (or `--url`); `--plain` prints only the token.
- The port is the workspace's preferred port, so the URL stays the same between runs. If it was taken, run `beam mcp setup --transport http` again.
- `--transport stdio` (default) writes a `dotnet beam mcp serve` entry instead, which needs no running server.

### Pre-connection discovery

| Route | Media type | Auth |
|---|---|---|
| `GET /.well-known/ai-catalog.json` | `application/ai-catalog+json` | none, CORS `*` |
| `GET /mcp/server-card` | `application/mcp-server-card+json` | none, CORS `*` |
| `GET /info` | `application/json` | none; `inflightCommands` only with the token |

The card's `remotes[0].supportedProtocolVersions` lists the revisions `/mcp` serves: `2026-07-28` (stateless, `server/discover`), and `2025-11-25`, `2025-06-18`, `2025-03-26` (initialize handshake with `Mcp-Session-Id`).

### Errors from `/mcp`

| Status | `type` | Meaning |
|---|---|---|
| 401 | `Unauthorized` | Missing or wrong `Authorization: Bearer <token>`. Re-run the headers helper. |
| 403 | `ForbiddenOrigin` | Request carried an `Origin` header |
| 403 | `ForbiddenHost` | `Host` was not `127.0.0.1:<port>` |
| 400 | `UnhandledRoute` | Server started without `--enable-mcp` |

### Tool results

`beam_exec` returns `isError: true` when the exit code is non-zero, an `error*` event was reported, or the call was cancelled. `structuredContent` is `{command, exitCode, events[]}`, with `events` in the same `ReportDataPoint` shape Unity receives (`{ts, type, data}`).
